To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the main objectives and sub-objectives, and then break them down into tasks. Here's how the goal model can be structured:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                    | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food                  | Ensure food is delivered to the inpatient room.                      | -                  | Perform   | -        |
| G2      | Determine Retrieval Method    | Decide how the food will be retrieved by the inpatient or others.    | FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2) | Query     | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Food to Table         | Deliver food directly to the room table using robot manipulation.    | -                  | Perform   | G2       |
| G4      | Coordinate Tray Retrieval     | Facilitate food retrieval from the robot's tray with assistance.     | FALLBACK(G4.1, G4.2) | Perform   | G2       |
| G5      | Track Meal Retrieval          | Track which meal is retrieved by whom and when.                      | #                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G6      | Alert on Wrong Meal Retrieval | Alert if the wrong meal is retrieved.                                | -                  | Achieve   | G5       |
| G7      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes         | Retrieve dirty dishes from the inpatient room.                       | -                  | Perform   | -        |
| G8      | Coordinate Dish Pickup        | Coordinate dish retrieval with or without assistance.               | FALLBACK(G8.1, G8.2) | Perform   | G7       |
| G9      | Open Room Door                | Ensure the room door is opened for robot entry.                      | FALLBACK(G9.1, G9.2) | Perform   | G7, G8   |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                   | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location       | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Room             | Move to the designated inpatient room.                              | AND      | Inpatient Room | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Execute Manipulation Skill   | Use robot skill to place food on the room table.                    | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT3     | Communicate with Inpatient   | Inform inpatient about meal retrieval options.                      | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT4     | Communicate with Companion/Nurse | Inform companion or nurse about meal retrieval options.            | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT5     | Coordinate with Another Robot| Work with another robot to assist in tray retrieval.                 | AND      | Inpatient Room | [2, n]           |
| AT6     | Track Meal Retrieval         | Log which meal is retrieved by whom and when.                        | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT7     | Alert on Wrong Retrieval     | Notify if the wrong meal is retrieved.                               | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT8     | Retrieve Dishes              | Collect dirty dishes from the room.                                  | AND      | Inpatient Room | [1, n]           |
| AT9     | Signal Door Status           | Check if the door can be opened by a person in the room.            | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT10    | Coordinate Dish Pickup with Human | Work with a human to pick up dishes.                             | AND      | Inpatient Room | [1, n]           |
| AT11    | Open Door                    | Open the door for robot entry.                                       | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G5 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G3, G4 [OR]**
- **G3 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**
- **G4 -> AT3, AT4, G4.1, G4.2 [FALLBACK]**
  - **G4.1 -> AT5 [AND]**
  - **G4.2 -> AT9, AT10 [FALLBACK]**
- **G5 -> AT6, G6 [PARALLEL]**
- **G7 -> G8, G9 [AND]**
- **G8 -> AT8, G8.1, G8.2 [FALLBACK]**
  - **G8.1 -> AT10 [AND]**
  - **G8.2 -> AT11 [AND]**
- **G9 -> AT9, AT11 [FALLBACK]**

This model ensures that the mission objectives are clearly defined and decomposed into actionable tasks, with logical relationships and execution structures specified.
